-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Evaluation and calibration text
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The evaluation inputs in openbonsai/eval/assets/bonsai-dev/ (frozen-inputs.json,
legacy-eval-inputs.json, chat-traces16.jsonl), the small example data in
examples/, and some reports under research/runs/ contain text excerpts from
the datasets below. The excerpts keep their original licenses; they are not
relicensed under Apache-2.0. Changes: excerpts were selected, tokenized with
the Qwen3.5 tokenizer and, for ARC, rendered as A/B/C/D multiple-choice
prompts; chat-traces16.jsonl holds Qwen3.5-9B answers to UltraChat prompts.
examples/tiny-data/ is original text written for the tests.

  WikiText-2 (raw), Salesforce/wikitext, revision
  b08601e04326c79dfdd32d625aee71d232d685c3.
  Stephen Merity, Caiming Xiong, James Bradbury, Richard Socher.
  "Pointer Sentinel Mixture Models", 2016.
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA 3.0).

  ARC-Easy (AI2 Reasoning Challenge), allenai/ai2_arc, revision
  210d026faf9955653af8916fad021475a3f00453.
  Peter Clark et al. "Think you have Solved Question Answering? Try ARC,
  the AI2 Reasoning Challenge", 2018.
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA 4.0).

  UltraChat 200k, HuggingFaceH4/ultrachat_200k (a filtered version of
  UltraChat by Ning Ding et al., "Enhancing Chat Language Models by Scaling
  High-quality Instructional Conversations", 2023). Used as calibration text.
  License: MIT.

The reasoning test subsets in openbonsai/eval/assets/reasoning/
(gsm8k-test-100.json, humaneval-test-50.json) hold problems copied unchanged
from the datasets below (selected rows; GSM8K reference solutions reduced to
their final number). They keep their original licenses (the copyright and
permission notices in the datasets' repositories apply).

  GSM8K, openai/gsm8k (main, test split), revision
  740312add88f781978c0658806c59bc2815b9866.
  Karl Cobbe et al. "Training Verifiers to Solve Math Word Problems", 2021.
  License: MIT.

  HumanEval, openai/openai_humaneval (test split), revision
  7dce6050a7d6d172f3cc5c32aa97f52fa1a2e544.
  Mark Chen et al. "Evaluating Large Language Models Trained on Code", 2021.
  License: MIT.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Qwen3.5
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Token IDs, chat-template markup, configuration fields and architecture
conventions follow Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B (revision
c202236235762e1c871ad0ccb60c8ee5ba337b9a), released by the Qwen team under
the Apache License 2.0. No Qwen model weights or tokenizer files are included.

